        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Coming to the offences under the IPC, the sections that are most often being pressed into service are Sections 272 and 273 IPC."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "74ba16e8d76246e3bf832cbc1b0607e3_14",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Section 272 IPC makes punishable an offence by a person, who adulterates any article of 'food or drink'."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "a37bdcdfa9ec414fb0e9d8756842cba9_15",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Therefore, this Section would only come into play if food or drink is adulterated."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "8448ca64c22849179fe0dc226a7ac305_16",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The Indian Penal Code does not describe or define adulteration."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "31838fa66bc04bab837de92c89e9071d_17",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The definition of adulterant is found in the provisions of the FSS Act."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "9141bdf5d0ae411d9f0300fdfb3a8f65_18",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "According to the said definition as found in Section 3(1)(a) of the FSS Act, adulterant is a material which could make the 'food' unsafe or sub-standard or mis-branded."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "6bd4a8000ed942f89c83d5a8d99db0e0_19",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Therefore, according to Section 272 IPC, if a material is used to make the food unsafe/sub-standard or mis-branded, then only the offence would be attracted."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "a861d43453844e4da43bddaee761c707_20",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In the case on hand, as tobacco or tobacco products do not come within the definition of food or drink, these products do not come within the ambit of Section 272 IPC."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "7d77c168f6de440e862d0b51fbda4116_21",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Similarly, Section 273 IPC talks of the sale of a noxious food or drink."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "9d30315694084281a3a4d4b6f9b40a0d_22",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "If a person offers for sale a \"food or drink\" any article which has become noxious or is in a state of unfit for \"food or drink\"."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "adab106c9fdb4361b4ddc6b7eb7ed73b_23",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "This section would apply, when an article which has become noxious or which has been rendered noxious."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "cc8215057a6146d79505e8ec39840de2_24",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It also applies to food or drink only."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "d4abdba65777472a8ee9832e6694c9cd_25",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The word 'noxious' is not defined in IPC, but as per the dictionary meaning noxious means harmful, deleterious, injurious, poisonous etc.\""
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "0896c04ca0af462a9c21b32d68bd7706_26",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "23. This Court's conclusion is that sale, manufacture, processing etc., of tobacco are not totally banned and in the latter part of the order this is discussed."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "f4f138db088a49d5a8f1db721fec4cc8_27",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Therefore, since the sale of tobacco products is still not banned in this country and it is only regulated to a certain extent, it cannot be said that Sections 269 and 270 IPC are attracted to a case of possession and sale of tobacco or tob"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "56502692efa349c289ea65505be2a3df_29",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "As per the decision in Uppara Veerendra (1 supra), tobacco is not food within the meaning of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 and a similar view is also expressed in Polisetty Srinivasa Rao (2 supra)."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "7f1122ec73154fec852263e901170a54_30",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "10. It is pertinent to mention that in circumstances similar to the case on hand (3 supra),\napplicability of many provisions of the Indian Penal Code fell for consideration and in view of the finding that tobacco is not food, the applicatio"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "87714d71aa234386b1fd59bb5ac44d5d_31",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS",
          "explicit_leakage_phrase"
        ],
